\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces SLV (top) and perplexity (bottom) across 10 recursive generations ($r{=}0$, 3-seed mean). In Phase~I (Gen~0--2), both metrics rise simultaneously. The SLV increase reflects distributional broadening, not model health. From Phase~III onward (Gen~4--10), the two metrics diverge: SLV declines monotonically while perplexity accelerates, which confirms that post-decompression SLV faithfully tracks structural collapse.}}{6}{figure.caption.17}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:slv_ppl_decoupling}{{4}{6}{SLV (top) and perplexity (bottom) across 10 recursive generations ($r{=}0$, 3-seed mean). In Phase~I (Gen~0--2), both metrics rise simultaneously. The SLV increase reflects distributional broadening, not model health. From Phase~III onward (Gen~4--10), the two metrics diverge: SLV declines monotonically while perplexity accelerates, which confirms that post-decompression SLV faithfully tracks structural collapse}{figure.caption.17}{}}
